// CRC-16, the common variants: https://reveng.sourceforge.io/crc-catalogue/
//
// The same shift-and-xor machine as CRC-32 with a 16-bit register, but the
// variants disagree about more than the polynomial: which way round the bits go,
// what the register starts at, and whether the answer is complemented at the
// end. Those four choices are what a CRC catalogue lists, and they are what this
// package parameterises rather than hard-coding one of them.
//
// A checksum, not a hash. It detects the burst errors a wire produces and
// detects nothing against someone who wants to change the message.
import {
  "moonbitstack/mooncrypt/spec",
}

import {
  "moonbitstack/moonbase/base16",
} for "test"
